31.0], [1242.0, 635.0], [1242.0, 665.0], [179.0, 661.0]], 'Surfactant use will be standardized on Curosurf (of 23 NICUs responding to a survey on', 0.986878864986952], [[[180.0, 668.0], [1281.0, 668.0], [1281.0, 697.0], [180.0, 697.0]], 'surfactant use, 13 use Curosurf, 7 Infasurf, and 7 Survanta - some use more than one; when', 0.9849436130788591], [[[180.0, 703.0], [1280.0, 703.0], [1280.0, 733.0], [180.0, 733.0]], 'asked if the study decides to use a single type, 17 NICUs were willing to use standard study', 0.9923989299846732], [[[179.0, 737.0], [1328.0, 736.0], [1328.0, 765.0], [179.0, 766.0]], 'surfactant, 3 were not willing - these 3 sites (NICUs) are from a single center and use Curosurf', 0.9886376603196064], [[[180.0, 770.0], [1338.0, 771.0], [1338.0, 801.0], [180.0, 800.0]], 'already and do not want to switch). An optional second dose of study drug may be administered,', 0.9962425821639121], [[[179.0, 806.0], [1097.0, 804.0], [1097.0, 834.0], [179.0, 836.0]], 'provided the second dose would be administered within 48+2 hours of birth.', 0.9971675880857416], [[[181.0, 870.0], [1320.0, 870.0], [1320.0, 900.0], [181.0, 900.0]], 'Suggested criteria for the initial dose of surfactant includes intubation of the infant with FiO2 >', 0.9903558787673411], [[[177.0, 901.0], [1338.0, 900.0], [1338.0, 936.0], [177.0, 937.0]], '0.25 to maintain SpO2 > 90%, or a PaCO2 > 65 torr at < 48h age. Suggested criteria for a second', 0.9939347524391977], [[[180.0, 938.0], [1272.0, 938.0], [1272.0, 971.0], [180.0, 971.0]], '(repeat) dose of study drug includes intubation of the infant at < 48h age with mean airway', 0.9855230074007433], [[[179.0, 974.0], [1201.0, 972.0], [1201.0, 1005.0], [179.0, 1007.0]], 'pressure > 6 cm H2O and FiO2 > 0.30 to maintain SpO2 > 90%, or a PaCO2 > 65 torr.', 0.9790771250371579], [[[180.0, 1033.0], [502.0, 1038.0], [502.0, 1074.0], [179.0, 1069.0]], '4.2.5. Blinding/Masking', 0.985251670298369], [[[181.0, 1088.0], [1273.0, 1088.0], [1273.0, 1117.0], [181.0, 1117.0]], 'This study will be masked, and all attempts will be made to maintain masking to the extent', 0.9893213364813063], [[[177.0, 1121.0], [1295.0, 1120.0], [1295.0, 1153.0], [177.0, 1154.0]], 'possible. Only research pharmacists and a designated respiratory therapist (or other qualified', 0.9972086263463852], [[[177.0, 1155.0], [1329.0, 1153.0], [1329.0, 1189.0], [177.0, 1191.0]], 'person) will be unmasked at the enrolling NICUs. The designated respiratory therapist (or other', 0.9864731688248484], [[[179.0, 1190.0], [1327.0, 1191.0], [1327.0, 1224.0], [179.0, 1223.0]], 'qualified person) must be unmasked to allow drug mixing at bedside for expeditious study drug', 0.9945181281335892], [[[178.0, 1224.0], [1307.0, 1226.0], [1307.0, 1258.0], [178.0, 1256.0]], 'administration; however, this person will not be the primary medical provider nor the primary', 0.9851617293973123], [[[181.0, 1260.0], [1136.0, 1260.0], [1136.0, 1289.0], [181.0, 1289.0]], 'data collector for that infant, and will not be otherwise involved in the research.', 0.9911357157201652], [[[180.0, 1323.0], [1322.0, 1323.0], [1322.0, 1356.0], [180.0, 1356.0]], "Each NICU's study-certified pharmacist will be responsible for tracking and documentation of", 0.9925348441237989], [[[182.0, 1360.0], [1268.0, 1359.0], [1268.0, 1389.0], [182.0, 1390.0]], 'study drug kits, as well as reporting directly to the DCC any protocol deviations/violations', 0.9933451297490493], [[[180.0, 1394.0], [774.0, 1394.0], [774.0, 1427.0], [180.0, 1427.0]], 'regarding unmasking on a designated study form.', 0.9947485657448464], [[[180.0, 1457.0], [1307.0, 1459.0], [1307.0, 1489.0], [180.0, 1487.0]], 'At the NICUs with bedside mixing, the mask will be preserved through use of drug kits. Drug', 0.9903390387912373], [[[181.0, 1493.0], [1289.0, 1493.0], [1289.0, 1523.0], [181.0, 1523.0]], 'kits will be prepared with budesonide or sham by the unmasked pharmacist and will be fully', 0.9870306134223938], [[[179.0, 1527.0], [1291.0, 1527.0], [1291.0, 1557.0], [179.0, 1557.0]], 'masked from the exterior in order to maintain masking of clinicians, research personnel, and', 0.9840121217395948], [[[180.0, 1562.0], [1264.0, 1562.0], [1264.0, 1592.0], [180.0, 1592.0]], 'families. The designated respiratory therapist (or other qualified person) will not know the', 0.9984458613654842], [[[177.0, 1595.0], [1337.0, 1594.0], [1337.0, 1627.0], [177.0, 1628.0]], 'randomized treatment arm prior to opening the drug kit. Once opened, the budesonide should be', 0.998026055033489], [[[179.0, 1630.0], [1321.0, 1632.0], [1321.0, 1662.0], [179.0, 1660.0]], 'mixed (or sham mimed to be mixed) with the surfactant by the same unmasked person. Mixing', 0.9895420724086548], [[[179.0, 1664.0], [1337.0, 1665.0], [1337.0, 1695.0], [179.0, 1694.0]], 'and administration should occur reasonably out of sight from masked individuals, and if needed,', 0.9931412947805305], [[[178.0, 1698.0], [1336.0, 1699.0], [1336.0, 1732.0], [178.0, 1730.0]], 'masking tape may be used to hide the total volume of the syringe used to administer the mixture', 0.9919140571042111], [[[180.0, 1733.0], [1313.0, 1733.0], [1313.0, 1766.0], [180.0, 1766.0]], '(budesonide does not change the appearance of the surfactant solution, although the volume is', 0.9960678418477377], [[[181.0, 1769.0], [1314.0, 1769.0], [1314.0, 1798.0], [181.0, 1798.0]], 'slightly higher when budesonide is added). Before intratracheal instillation, the syringe will be', 0.9927519682756404], [[[748.0, 1861.0], [783.0, 1861.0], [783.0, 1891.0], [748.0, 1891.0]], '19', 0.9995701909065247]]
